          "prompt": "From: Buddy Williams <buddy.williams@insurity.com>\nSubject: Refine goal-agent stalls ~15 min on completion signal �X invalid no_change_needed outcome triggers stop-hook retry loop\n\nBody:\nTeam,\r\n\r\n  Heads-up on a Refine failure mode we hit on run 8082 (node BO2LNXNEVO03) that looks like a hang but isn't.\r\n\r\n  Symptom: A goal agent went silent for ~900 seconds with no output, then died. It looks like a network/compute hang or a stuck build.\r\n\r\n  Actual cause: The agent had already finished the work successfully �X solution built clean (0 errors, 0 StyleCop warnings), Systema.Sims.Data.Claims.Tdd 3/3 and Api.Tdd 385/385 passing. It\r\n  then tried to emit its Refine completion signal and got stuck in a schema-rejection loop:\r\n\r\n  �k Refine rejected your completion signal: does not match the required schema: implementation_evidence.checklist[2].outcome: unknown variant \"no_change_needed\", expected one of completed,\r\n  �k deviated, rejected, blocked. (replacement attempt 1 of 3).\r\n\r\n  The agent used outcome: \"no_change_needed\", which is not a valid value in the goal-agent signal schema �X that value only exists in the code-review/ReportFindings schema, and the agent\r\n  conflated the two. Each rejection forces a rewrite and re-runs the stop hook (~3m46s per cycle, visible in the logs as repeated running stop hook �P 3m 46s / Cooked for 3m 46s). Three retry\r\n  attempts �� ~4 min each, with no user-visible output in between, is where the ~15 minutes went. It never produced a valid signal, so the process ended as .log.failed.\r\n\r\n  What it is NOT:\r\n  - Not a network or compute hang.\r\n  - Not disk �X the \"No space left on device\" line in older run logs is a July incident; disk is currently at 44% used / 8% inodes.\r\n  - Not the build or tests �X those were green before the loop started.\r\n\r\n  Two things worth fixing on the Refine side:\r\n  1. Fail fast on invalid enum. An unknown outcome variant should be rejected immediately, not put through 3�� full stop-hook cycles (~12 min wasted per occurrence). The stop hook shouldn't run\r\n  on a signal that fails basic schema validation.\r\n  2. Enum mismatch across schemas. no_change_needed is valid in the review/findings schema but not the goal-agent completion schema. Either align the enums or make the rejection message name\r\n  the exact allowed values up front (it does list them �X but the agent still needs the schemas to stop diverging).\r\n\r\n\r\n�w�wAlso seen in the same run (separate issue):�wworking-tree�wcollisions�wskipped�wthe�wcheckout�wsync�w�X�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w\r\n  Entry 'Modules/Claims/Systema.Sims/.../ClaimBiz.cs' would be overwritten by merge �X leaving the integration delta \"staged-reverse until repair_pending_checkout_sync succeeds.\" Not the cause\r\n  of the stall, but the human checkout won't cleanly reflect the integrated change until that repair runs.\r\n\r\n  Practical takeaway: If you see a goal agent go quiet for ~15 min and then fail, check run/<id>/processes/goal-agent-*.stdout.log.failed for a \"rejected your completion signal\" loop before\r\n  assuming an infrastructure hang. The underlying task may already be complete.\r\n\r\n  Thanks,\r\n  Buddy\r\n\r\n\r\n[cid:insurity-small2_2f81c33c-d951-4e5c-a467-1113541ca22c.jpg]\r\nBuddy Williams\r\nBuddy.Williams@insurity.com\r\n\r\n[cid:excellence2026signature(17b0688e-5473-4b74-96eb-a73f633f2c2f)_48407359-d77b-4967-95cd-277a32b50ebc.png]<https://insurity.com/excellence?utm_source=Email-Signature&utm_medium=Email&utm_campaign=Event-Excellence-2026>\r\n\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this e-mail message is intended only for the personal and confidential use of the intended recipient(s). This message may be an attorney-client communication and/or work product and as such is privileged and confidential. If the reader of this message is not the intended recipient or an agent responsible for delivering it to the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that you have received this document in error and that any review, dissemination, distribution, or copying of this message is strictly prohibited. If you have received this communication in error, please notify us immediately by e-mail, and delete the original message.\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n~~~Insurity~~~",
